  "body": "**What is this feature?**\n\nThis pull request fixes a UI bug in the Alerting unified rule editor where the `Max data points` and `Min interval` options fail to save if the user clicks outside the tooltip to close it.\n\n**Why do we need this feature?**\n\nIn the current implementation, `MaxDataPointsOption` and `MinIntervalOption` components rely exclusively on the `onBlur` event of the `<Input />` field to trigger the `onChange` callback and save their values. Because these options are rendered inside a `Toggletip` component, clicking anywhere outside the tooltip immediately unmounts its children. Unmounting an element before its blur phase is completed often drops the blur event, causing any newly typed values to be discarded.\n\nThis fix introduces an explicit \"Apply\" button within the tooltip. Rather than implicitly attempting to persist data on blur or unmount—which was prone to being lost during the time-picker's unmount cycle—the `MaxDataPointsOption` and `MinIntervalOption` components now use local state tied to `onChange` events. When the user modifies these values, they must explicitly click \"Apply\" to validate and sync the changes to the query model. Clicking outside the tooltip will gracefully discard unapplied changes. It also includes comprehensive unit tests to prevent regressions.\n\n**Who is this feature for?**\n\nGrafana users and administrators authoring or editing Alert rules who use the options tooltip to configure query evaluation intervals and data points.\n\n**Which issue(s) does this PR fix?**:\n\nFixes #111664\n\n**Special notes for your reviewer:**\n\nPlease check that:\n- [x] It works as expected from a user's perspective.\n- [ ] If this is a pre-GA feature, it is behind a feature toggle. *(Not applicable)*\n- [ ] The docs are updated, and if this is a [notable improvement](https://grafana.com/docs/writers-toolkit/contribute/release-notes/#how-to-determine-if-content-belongs-in-whats-new), it's added to our [What's New](https://grafana.com/docs/writers-toolkit/contribute/release-notes/) doc. *(Not applicable)*",
